From c3c54bab3d2794004f374f8ce8d16e8cd3a28949 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:23:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Occlusion queries measured with Metal visibility results
 (VPVK_OCCLUSION, default on)

- core: Draw::visibility (one 8-byte slot per queried draw), GpuTimings::visibility,
  Device::frameVisibility (last 64 frames).
- metal2: a 64 KB visibility buffer per frame slot, zeroed on the host before use;
  render passes of a frame with queried draws bind it; MTLVisibilityResultModeCounting
  at the draw's slot; slots no draw was encoded for (or an errored frame) read 1.
- vulkan: vkCmdBeginQuery/EndQuery tag the recorded draws (occlusion pools); the
  translator gives each a slot (cap 8192 per submission, beyond = unknown = visible);
  stampQueries keeps the query's slots; vkGetQueryPoolResults sums the counts, 0 for a
  query without draws, 1 when anything is unknown. Before: every occlusion query read 1.
